## 6. User Roles and Permissions

Support three roles:

### Student
Students can:
* Manage their own student profile.
* Search and filter the alumni directory.
* View eligible alumni profiles.
* Send mentorship requests.
* View the status of their requests.
* Communicate with connected or accepted mentors.
* Book mentorship sessions where permitted.
* View their bookings.
* Browse opportunities.
* Apply for opportunities.
* Track their own applications.
* View notifications.
* Update personal settings.

### Alumni
Alumni can:
* Manage their own professional profile.
* View and manage mentorship requests addressed to them.
* Accept or reject mentorship requests.
* Communicate with authorized students.
* Offer and manage mentorship sessions.
* View their own bookings.
* Create, update, and manage their opportunities.
* View applications submitted to their opportunities.
* Update availability and account settings.
* Receive notifications.

### Administrator
Administrators can:
* Access a protected administration dashboard.
* View platform statistics.
* Review pending alumni verification requests.
* Approve or reject alumni verification with a recorded reason.
* Manage users and account status.
* Moderate opportunities.
* Review reports or inappropriate content.
* View relevant audit records.

An administrator must not be able to create arbitrary sessions or impersonate users through an unprotected endpoint.

Do not provide public administrator registration. Seed an administrator through a secure, documented server-side setup process.

